WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.290
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:10.560 --> 00:13.530
Give us a quick recap. What happened in Phetchabun?

3
00:14.100 --> 00:16.960
The trip was full of cuteness, dude!

4
00:17.560 --> 00:18.640
I think...

5
00:18.660 --> 00:20.170
I'm gonna make a move on Jane.

6
00:20.950 --> 00:22.130
And do you think he has feelings for you?

7
00:22.380 --> 00:23.470
How would I know?

8
00:23.750 --> 00:26.170
You two were alone together for two nights.

9
00:26.960 --> 00:28.440
Did you do anything that might have

10
00:29.170 --> 00:30.650
ignited the romance?

11
00:31.660 --> 00:33.050
Spending time with you

12
00:33.460 --> 00:35.600
makes my life seem a lot simpler.

13
00:36.260 --> 00:38.150
Stay with me for a long time, okay?

14
00:38.270 --> 00:39.350
Don't leave.

15
00:46.280 --> 00:47.470
Here you go.

16
00:48.160 --> 00:49.340
It's piping hot.

17
00:49.360 --> 00:51.600
Eat up. It'll make you feel better.

18
00:54.050 --> 00:55.170
Isn't it embarrassing,

19
00:55.360 --> 00:56.650
the state we're in?

20
00:58.640 --> 01:00.830
I don't think I drank that much last night.

21
01:01.080 --> 01:02.500
Why is my head hurting so badly?

22
01:04.350 --> 01:05.770
What the hell are you talking about?

23
01:06.360 --> 01:08.100
Your eyes were brimming with alcohol.

24
01:08.240 --> 01:09.560
Jeez...

25
01:09.760 --> 01:11.820
Your head was literally inside a toilet bowl.

26
01:11.850 --> 01:13.100
And you're roasting me?

27
01:26.660 --> 01:27.940
A compensation

28
01:28.050 --> 01:29.800
for getting us into the car last night.

29
01:32.360 --> 01:33.770
It's totally fine.

30
01:34.040 --> 01:35.200
It was fun, actually.

31
01:40.800 --> 01:41.560
Hey!

32
01:42.620 --> 01:44.130
Am I missing out on something?

33
01:44.660 --> 01:45.470
Give me an update now!

34
01:45.740 --> 01:48.000
Well... It's nothing, actually.

35
01:50.470 --> 01:52.770
She's not talking about you.

36
01:54.270 --> 01:55.000
Really?

37
01:55.830 --> 01:57.470
Oh, okay. I'm sorry, then.

38
02:01.640 --> 02:02.770
That was close...

39
02:07.560 --> 02:09.530
You almost screwed yourself up.

40
02:10.200 --> 02:11.070
Just eat!

41
02:15.380 --> 02:16.300
Jaab, dig in already.

42
02:16.670 --> 02:17.860
Alright.

43
04:00.500 --> 04:03.370
[At what moment do we start falling for someone?]

44
04:07.450 --> 04:11.730
"At what moment do we start falling for someone?"

45
04:15.350 --> 04:16.700
This would be it!

46
04:18.170 --> 04:18.740
Huh!

47
04:20.270 --> 04:21.140
Jane!

48
04:21.650 --> 04:23.020
You're being rude!

49
04:23.040 --> 04:24.960
You're peeking at someone else's work.

50
04:25.750 --> 04:28.730
Khanoon said you're making changes to the MV.

51
04:29.210 --> 04:30.840
But if this is rude,

52
04:30.860 --> 04:32.660
then I'll get back to doing nothing...

53
04:32.680 --> 04:34.250
Wait, Jane.

54
04:34.270 --> 04:36.930
Come on... Don't be upset, you tiny boy.

55
04:37.740 --> 04:39.160
I'd like you, Mr. Jannarong,

56
04:39.180 --> 04:41.830
to offer me your assistance.

57
04:48.850 --> 04:50.530
Khanoon asked if I wanted noodles.

58
04:50.550 --> 04:51.460
Do you want some?

59
04:51.480 --> 04:52.730
The hot soup will sober you up.

60
04:53.950 --> 04:55.100
Um...

61
04:55.540 --> 04:56.540
I'm good.

62
04:56.560 --> 04:58.170
I had porridge already this morning.

63
04:58.190 --> 04:59.770
They're both soupy.

64
04:59.980 --> 05:01.650
I prefer something with rice.

65
05:12.410 --> 05:13.330
Jane.

66
05:14.480 --> 05:15.480
Well...

67
05:16.760 --> 05:19.570
I can't recall much from last night.

68
05:19.670 --> 05:21.530
Did I say something strange?

69
05:27.030 --> 05:28.200
You're asking me that again.

70
05:29.070 --> 05:30.800
You asked me the same thing this morning.

71
05:33.170 --> 05:36.370
Do you usually do weird stuff when you forget yourself?

72
05:37.360 --> 05:38.270
Uh...

73
05:38.860 --> 05:39.930
No, Jane.

74
05:39.950 --> 05:42.050
I just wanted to make sure.

75
05:42.070 --> 05:45.650
I don't want to act like a clown and ruin this handsome look.

76
05:51.760 --> 05:53.650
Last night, I was also super drunk.

77
05:54.360 --> 05:57.400
I wasn't doing anything weird around you, right?

78
05:58.970 --> 06:02.460
Have you ever... loved someone?

79
06:03.550 --> 06:05.100
Have you ever been in a relationship?

80
06:06.270 --> 06:07.370
Jane...

81
06:07.970 --> 06:08.950
Why did you ask me that?

82
06:09.460 --> 06:11.070
When you feel that you...

83
06:11.610 --> 06:13.490
love someone

84
06:14.060 --> 06:16.040
who isn't your family,

85
06:16.060 --> 06:17.800
not a tree,

86
06:18.470 --> 06:19.860
not Auntie Kaew,

87
06:20.650 --> 06:22.050
what does it feel like?

88
06:22.930 --> 06:24.470
Are you...

89
06:25.360 --> 06:26.780
having...

90
06:26.800 --> 06:28.360
a crush on someone?

91
06:34.660 --> 06:36.000
You're quiet.

92
06:36.350 --> 06:37.070
I totally did.

93
06:37.350 --> 06:38.580
No... Jane.

94
06:38.600 --> 06:39.650
You didn't do anything!

95
06:40.340 --> 06:41.450
Tell me.

96
06:41.470 --> 06:44.130
Was I acting weird around you without knowing?

97
06:45.070 --> 06:46.700
It wasn't weird, Jane.

98
06:47.060 --> 06:47.870
It wasn't.

99
06:48.120 --> 06:50.360
If it wasn't weird, then what did I do?

100
06:50.730 --> 06:51.670
Well...

101
06:52.650 --> 06:53.650
You told me that...

102
06:54.200 --> 06:55.400
I...

103
06:59.150 --> 07:01.490
I don't remember much, Jane.

104
07:01.510 --> 07:02.270
Like I...

105
07:02.650 --> 07:04.670
I was also very drunk. Yeah.

106
07:10.460 --> 07:12.180
Are you sure that it was nothing?

107
07:12.460 --> 07:14.060
You didn't record anything, did you?

108
07:15.840 --> 07:17.350
I wish I had...

109
07:22.050 --> 07:23.000
- Jaab! - Whoa!

110
07:23.140 --> 07:23.930
Spill it out!

111
07:24.070 --> 07:25.580
You didn't do anything, Jane.

112
07:26.070 --> 07:26.640
I swear.

113
07:26.770 --> 07:27.380
With...

114
07:27.900 --> 07:29.070
On my kitty cat's honor.

115
07:29.650 --> 07:30.370
I don't believe you!

116
07:30.390 --> 07:31.560
You didn't do anything, Jane.

117
07:31.580 --> 07:33.080
- I swear. - Jane. Jaab.

118
07:33.640 --> 07:35.050
- What is it, Ai? - Uh...

119
07:35.140 --> 07:39.280
Chomphoo sent me to tell you that the meeting this afternoon is canceled.

120
07:39.300 --> 07:41.740
Bew hasn't gotten better, so she can't make it here.

121
07:41.760 --> 07:42.600
Yes!

122
07:43.560 --> 07:45.030
That's what I'm talking about!

123
07:46.260 --> 07:47.800
Thank you, Ai.

124
07:47.870 --> 07:48.860
No problem.

125
07:52.050 --> 07:52.760
Hey.

126
07:53.340 --> 07:54.850
You're having so much fun with these, huh?

127
07:56.770 --> 07:58.420
- There. Squishy. - Ow, Jane!

128
07:58.440 --> 08:00.360
- Jane! It hurts! - Squishy!

129
08:00.380 --> 08:01.760
Jane, it hurts!

130
08:16.930 --> 08:17.570
Whoa...

131
08:17.870 --> 08:18.480
Jane.

132
08:18.500 --> 08:19.260
Well...

133
08:19.560 --> 08:20.350
I...

134
08:20.890 --> 08:21.890
I'm hungry now.

135
08:22.550 --> 08:24.220
Can you help me pick my lunch?

136
08:24.240 --> 08:26.210
I... I can't come up with anything.

137
08:26.230 --> 08:28.890
Nothing soupy, though.

138
08:29.350 --> 08:30.490
Can you order something for me, too?

139
08:31.960 --> 08:32.810
Huh?

140
08:34.040 --> 08:35.560
You didn't order noodles with Khanoon.

141
08:35.580 --> 08:37.120
I thought you brought your own lunch.

142
08:40.870 --> 08:42.860
Getting out of bed was already hard enough.

143
08:43.560 --> 08:45.600
I didn't even have the energy to press the microwave buttons.

144
08:48.260 --> 08:49.260
But...

145
08:49.750 --> 08:51.370
I don't want anything soupy either.

146
08:51.870 --> 08:53.150
If that's so...

147
08:53.170 --> 08:54.800
how about we eat out?

148
09:26.560 --> 09:27.270
Let's go, Jane.

149
10:12.870 --> 10:14.070
Whoa, Jane, Jane!

150
10:17.070 --> 10:17.960
Hey!

151
10:18.260 --> 10:19.260
You call that riding?!

152
10:29.870 --> 10:31.070
Why are you doing this?

153
10:31.860 --> 10:32.970
Why, Jane?

154
10:33.160 --> 10:34.600
I'm shielding you from the traffic.

155
10:36.320 --> 10:38.460
We're on the sidewalk.

156
10:38.760 --> 10:40.800
It doesn't matter.

157
10:40.950 --> 10:42.840
Why wouldn't it matter, Jane?

158
10:42.860 --> 10:43.610
The footpath is dangerous...

159
11:12.970 --> 11:14.500
Any side of the road is...

160
11:15.470 --> 11:18.000
just as dangerous.

161
11:18.570 --> 11:19.570
So please...

162
11:20.170 --> 11:22.870
live more carefully.

163
11:28.180 --> 11:29.000
Well...

164
11:29.360 --> 11:31.340
How am I not careful, Jane?

165
11:32.450 --> 11:33.250
Well...

166
11:33.450 --> 11:35.900
Eyes on the road. Don't always look at me.

167
11:38.650 --> 11:40.970
And how did you know that I was only looking at you?

168
11:41.500 --> 11:42.840
Or were you also...

169
11:42.950 --> 11:44.850
only looking at me?

170
11:45.650 --> 11:47.830
You're as tall as a durian tree.

171
11:48.060 --> 11:49.260
You're always in my sight.

172
11:50.350 --> 11:51.170
Huh!

173
11:51.740 --> 11:52.330
Whoa!

174
11:54.240 --> 11:56.950
Jane, that scared me.

175
11:56.970 --> 11:57.860
Give me a hug, please.

176
11:57.890 --> 11:58.740
Hey...

177
11:59.950 --> 12:01.400
- Come on. I'm hungry. - Oh, Jane.

178
12:02.580 --> 12:03.530
Little bean sprout!

179
12:04.260 --> 12:05.700
Wait for this durian, please.

180
12:06.750 --> 12:07.840
Bean sprout!

181
12:18.060 --> 12:20.320
If others found out that we're having lunch at a mall,

182
12:20.550 --> 12:22.540
wouldn't they be mad that we didn't invite them?

183
12:23.400 --> 12:24.460
It's okay.

184
12:24.480 --> 12:26.210
They're eating noodles with Khanoon.

185
12:34.860 --> 12:35.860
And...

186
12:36.560 --> 12:38.080
Do you like Japanese food, Jane?

187
12:39.250 --> 12:40.250
It's fine.

188
12:45.960 --> 12:47.210
What do you like?

189
12:47.360 --> 12:49.550
Like, your favorite ones.

190
12:51.500 --> 12:52.700
Why are you asking me this?

191
12:53.960 --> 12:54.960
Well, I...

192
12:55.350 --> 12:56.530
I just want to know.

193
12:56.550 --> 12:57.670
Can't I?

194
13:00.660 --> 13:01.750
I'm not telling you.

195
13:02.050 --> 13:03.250
Or else you'll do the same thing Min does.

196
13:05.400 --> 13:06.400
What do you mean?

197
13:09.730 --> 13:10.730
I don't know why,

198
13:11.150 --> 13:13.400
but everyone around me likes to spoil me.

199
13:13.840 --> 13:15.650
I told Min about my favorite food, right?

200
13:15.910 --> 13:17.530
And she just keeps treating me to it.

201
13:18.430 --> 13:21.070
She never picks the food she wants.

202
13:22.250 --> 13:23.020
Really...?

203
13:24.550 --> 13:25.670
Maybe it's because

204
13:25.870 --> 13:27.560
you're endearing?

205
13:28.350 --> 13:29.870
Endearing,

206
13:30.350 --> 13:31.670
adorable,

207
13:32.240 --> 13:33.240
and sweet.

208
13:34.230 --> 13:35.400
Something like that.

209
13:37.760 --> 13:39.550
And what's your favorite food?

210
13:40.850 --> 13:44.300
And... why are you asking me that?

211
13:44.860 --> 13:45.860
What?

212
13:45.880 --> 13:47.130
I want to know it first,

213
13:47.250 --> 13:49.130
so that I can spoil you later.

214
13:57.080 --> 14:00.260
And why do you want to spoil me?

215
14:08.440 --> 14:10.970
Alright. Let me get this for you.

216
14:11.070 --> 14:11.850
Here.

217
14:12.460 --> 14:13.460
It's really good.

218
14:13.850 --> 14:15.330
Try it.

219
14:29.610 --> 14:30.510
Jaab.

220
14:30.680 --> 14:31.510
Hm?

221
14:32.950 --> 14:34.600
After studying film,

222
14:35.050 --> 14:36.770
are movies less enjoyable for you?

223
14:39.040 --> 14:40.040
Way less.

224
14:40.960 --> 14:43.080
Back then, I only watched them for fun, right?

225
14:43.100 --> 14:45.360
But after studying film, I can't stop analyzing everything.

226
14:45.390 --> 14:47.170
The compositions and the emotions.

227
14:47.760 --> 14:49.200
It's like the theater itself is my classroom.

228
14:50.360 --> 14:51.750
It's the same for me.

229
14:52.150 --> 14:53.830
Studying film...

230
14:54.250 --> 14:55.560
makes me enjoy movies less.

231
14:56.660 --> 14:59.050
I can't even remember the last time I went to a movie theater.

232
15:02.450 --> 15:03.930
I also...

233
15:03.950 --> 15:06.040
haven't gone to a theater in such a long time.

234
15:06.570 --> 15:07.870
How about we...

235
15:08.270 --> 15:09.440
watch a movie together?

236
15:09.470 --> 15:10.860
But we have to get back to the office.

237
15:14.660 --> 15:15.370
Fine.

238
15:20.870 --> 15:23.480
Maybe next time. Let's pick a date, too.

239
15:26.150 --> 15:27.150
Sure!

240
15:28.650 --> 15:29.960
You said it yourself.

241
15:30.470 --> 15:31.470
Mm.

242
15:32.900 --> 15:33.960
Okay.

243
15:34.220 --> 15:36.400
That's a promise. You can't take it back now.

244
15:41.760 --> 15:43.270
Have you ever tried those machines, Jaab?

245
15:44.250 --> 15:45.400
Of course, Jane.

246
15:45.470 --> 15:46.850
Everyone has tried them, no?

247
15:46.970 --> 15:48.140
Back in high school,

248
15:48.160 --> 15:50.960
I spent all of my allowance on those things.

249
15:54.670 --> 15:56.200
Everyone but...

250
15:56.610 --> 15:59.790
this homeschooled country kid.

251
16:05.860 --> 16:06.960
Well, then...

252
16:07.360 --> 16:08.600
Wanna give it a try?

253
16:11.360 --> 16:13.040
Lunchtime is almost over.

254
16:13.060 --> 16:13.920
I don't want to be late.

255
16:14.050 --> 16:15.000
Hey...

256
16:15.080 --> 16:16.260
Trust me.

257
16:16.280 --> 16:17.120
It won't take long.

258
16:18.040 --> 16:19.440
Jane, let's do this!

259
16:21.220 --> 16:22.800
Come on, trust me. Let's go.

260
16:25.450 --> 16:26.450
Here, Jane.

261
16:26.650 --> 16:27.650
Give it a try.

262
16:31.160 --> 16:33.330
Aim for the center, okay?

263
16:33.350 --> 16:35.000
Three... Two...

264
16:35.020 --> 16:35.720
One! Go!

265
16:37.760 --> 16:38.510
Jane!

266
16:38.530 --> 16:40.530
Amazing, Jane! Let's go!

267
16:41.920 --> 16:43.250
Yeah, beautiful.

268
16:53.330 --> 16:54.650
Jane, wanna try?

269
16:54.670 --> 16:55.580
Come here.

270
16:56.140 --> 16:56.960
Come on.

271
16:56.980 --> 16:58.450
- I can't dance. - Just give it a try.

272
16:58.470 --> 17:00.450
Don't be shy. People will watch either way.

273
17:05.340 --> 17:07.720
Go, go, go.

274
17:07.860 --> 17:09.240
Spin, spin, spin.

275
17:09.660 --> 17:10.400
Go.

276
17:16.240 --> 17:17.440
Hit it. Hit it. Hit.

277
17:17.460 --> 17:19.120
Go, go, go.

278
17:20.790 --> 17:22.080
There. Hit there.

279
17:22.110 --> 17:23.360
Jane, Jane, Jane!

280
17:23.380 --> 17:24.470
This one. This.

281
17:25.090 --> 17:26.700
They're not popping up anymore. Oh, there.

282
17:50.050 --> 17:50.880
Is it good?

283
17:51.660 --> 17:53.740
Wait, where are those two?

284
17:54.450 --> 17:55.450
Haven't seen them.

285
17:55.850 --> 17:56.560
Huh.

286
17:56.670 --> 17:57.840
Where are they?

287
17:57.870 --> 17:58.480
Huh?

288
18:00.160 --> 18:01.740
Maybe they're on a date?

289
18:03.510 --> 18:04.440
Seriously?

290
18:04.460 --> 18:05.480
I don't know.

291
18:09.680 --> 18:10.760
There they are.

292
18:10.780 --> 18:12.640
Speak of the devil.

293
18:12.660 --> 18:14.260
Ai, I brought you some treats.

294
18:14.540 --> 18:15.360
Thank you.

295
18:27.350 --> 18:28.260
- Hey. - Hm?

296
18:28.280 --> 18:29.280
What are you two signaling?

297
18:29.760 --> 18:30.780
What do you mean?

298
18:30.800 --> 18:31.680
I wasn't doing anything.

299
18:31.700 --> 18:32.570
Nothing!

300
18:32.590 --> 18:33.840
You must be seeing things.

301
18:35.150 --> 18:36.630
I wasn't signaling anything.

302
18:36.650 --> 18:37.780
Nothing at all.

303
18:43.370 --> 18:45.360
The ride got canceled again.

304
18:48.750 --> 18:49.770
That's how it is, Jane.

305
18:49.790 --> 18:50.750
We're in the heart of the city.

306
18:50.780 --> 18:52.160
It's rush hour, too.

307
18:58.000 --> 18:59.320
I'm sleepy already...

308
19:05.860 --> 19:06.600
So...

309
19:06.860 --> 19:09.360
at what moment do we start falling for someone?

310
19:09.570 --> 19:10.350
Huh?!

311
19:11.270 --> 19:12.270
Jane...

312
19:13.050 --> 19:14.280
What are you talking about?

313
19:15.360 --> 19:16.760
I'm talking about the MV.

314
19:17.350 --> 19:18.600
How about we come up with some ideas

315
19:19.300 --> 19:20.020
while we're waiting for our ride?

316
19:20.040 --> 19:21.220
So we won't waste time.

317
19:24.150 --> 19:25.560
Gosh, Jane.

318
19:25.580 --> 19:27.160
Next time, make it clear.

319
19:27.460 --> 19:28.460
Saying that out of the blue,

320
19:28.750 --> 19:30.280
you made my heart jump.

321
19:32.050 --> 19:34.160
You go first. I'll type it down.

322
19:34.970 --> 19:35.880
Well, then...

323
19:35.900 --> 19:37.320
How about we take turns?

324
19:37.340 --> 19:38.800
This way, we'll get various answers.

325
19:43.940 --> 19:45.480
Maybe it's the moment when the eyes meet.

326
19:56.340 --> 19:59.800
The moment when someone cares about little details.

327
20:01.870 --> 20:03.600
They are fully themselves when they're around each other.

328
20:04.140 --> 20:05.840
They feel at ease whenever they're together.

329
20:06.740 --> 20:09.120
They feel like this person is the first one to share stories with.

330
20:22.490 --> 20:23.750
The more they look at that person...

331
20:24.170 --> 20:25.440
the deeper they fall in love.

332
20:29.240 --> 20:32.080
The moment when they yearn for that person all of a sudden.

333
20:33.440 --> 20:34.230
How's that?

334
20:44.670 --> 20:45.670
That works.

335
20:52.040 --> 20:53.340
What else?

336
20:57.480 --> 20:58.650
Well...

337
20:59.740 --> 21:00.960
The moment when...

338
21:03.670 --> 21:05.450
one is happy that their ride got canceled.

339
21:05.550 --> 21:07.760
- So the two of them will have more time... - Hello?

340
21:08.040 --> 21:10.500
Oh, you can head inside the building.

341
21:11.470 --> 21:12.560
Okay.

342
21:15.210 --> 21:16.360
Jaab, we've got a ride.

343
21:18.140 --> 21:18.920
Really?

344
21:20.040 --> 21:21.040
Yay...

345
21:21.950 --> 21:23.570
Oh, by the way...

346
21:23.590 --> 21:25.720
what was the last one again?

347
21:26.960 --> 21:27.750
I...

348
21:28.140 --> 21:29.120
said...

349
21:29.470 --> 21:30.560
Hello?

350
21:31.940 --> 21:32.650
Okay. Sure.

351
21:32.670 --> 21:33.640
Just a moment, please.

352
21:34.150 --> 21:34.870
Jaab, our ride's here.

353
21:34.890 --> 21:35.580
Let's go.

354
21:40.280 --> 21:41.440
It's the moment...

355
21:42.050 --> 21:43.480
I get to be with you, Jane.

356
21:46.180 --> 21:47.280
Jaab, come on.

357
21:48.050 --> 21:49.050
Alright!

358
21:54.720 --> 21:58.520
[Jane]

359
22:28.960 --> 22:29.790
Oh...

360
22:30.370 --> 22:31.200
Jaab.

361
22:31.980 --> 22:33.800
Why are you so close to the screen?

362
22:35.830 --> 22:37.680
Why did you call me, kiddo?

363
22:40.160 --> 22:40.910
Whoa!

364
22:41.060 --> 22:42.680
You just got out of the shower, too?

365
22:44.950 --> 22:46.720
I was wondering about the last one.

366
22:47.480 --> 22:48.880
What do you mean? The last one?

367
22:49.050 --> 22:51.640
What we talked about while we were waiting for the ride.

368
22:52.250 --> 22:54.680
I wasn't listening to your last example.

369
22:54.970 --> 22:56.560
I wanted to ask you in the car, but I forgot.

370
22:57.050 --> 22:59.980
Oh, about that...

371
23:01.450 --> 23:03.050
Mm...

372
23:04.570 --> 23:05.600
I forgot.

373
23:05.870 --> 23:06.870
Completely forgot.

374
23:07.260 --> 23:08.520
I don't remember.

375
23:08.770 --> 23:09.770
Think harder.

376
23:12.870 --> 23:13.680
I...

377
23:14.170 --> 23:16.260
I forgot about it, Jane.

378
23:16.280 --> 23:18.250
Plus, for that MV,

379
23:18.270 --> 23:19.840
we only need a few examples.

380
23:19.860 --> 23:21.640
You already gave me plenty.

381
23:22.160 --> 23:23.360
Did I?

382
23:23.380 --> 23:25.960
I'll text them to you, okay?

383
23:26.130 --> 23:27.080
Mm.

384
23:29.000 --> 23:29.660
Oh.

385
23:30.530 --> 23:31.950
Are you telling the story in retrospect, Jaab?

386
23:32.230 --> 23:34.420
Oh, you mean the MV?

387
23:34.440 --> 23:35.280
Mm.

388
23:36.920 --> 23:39.360
You were looking for the starting moments of a relationship

389
23:39.380 --> 23:40.760
for the end of the MV.

390
23:44.070 --> 23:45.270
Oh.

391
23:45.840 --> 23:46.640
Yeah.

392
23:47.170 --> 23:50.200
My goal is to include good moments at the end.

393
23:50.480 --> 23:51.920
Good and sweet moments that...

394
23:52.270 --> 23:53.760
one cannot go back to

395
23:53.780 --> 23:55.720
no matter how much they miss them.

396
23:58.080 --> 23:59.080
I think...

397
23:59.560 --> 24:01.760
the vibe will be even sadder

398
24:01.780 --> 24:03.280
than the misunderstanding trope.

399
24:03.880 --> 24:04.920
That's what I think.

400
24:05.440 --> 24:07.360
You're such a mean director.

401
24:07.970 --> 24:09.880
You're not going to spare the audience the pain?

402
24:09.900 --> 24:11.040
Come on, Jane.

403
24:11.060 --> 24:12.620
It has to feel realistic, alright?

404
24:12.640 --> 24:13.650
It has to make them...

405
24:14.800 --> 24:17.440
cry their eyes out.

406
24:18.800 --> 24:20.320
Like, "Why is it so sad?"

407
24:20.570 --> 24:21.440
Something like that.

408
24:26.150 --> 24:27.280
Have you put on the blanket?

409
24:32.640 --> 24:33.400
Mm.

410
24:33.740 --> 24:34.600
Yes.

411
24:35.250 --> 24:35.960
Mm.

412
24:36.270 --> 24:37.400
You should go to bed, then.

413
24:38.150 --> 24:39.660
I'm already in bed.

414
24:40.160 --> 24:41.320
That's not what I meant.

415
24:41.560 --> 24:42.920
I mean, you should...

416
24:45.660 --> 24:46.600
Like this.

417
24:49.040 --> 24:49.960
I'm hanging up, okay?

418
24:50.670 --> 24:51.520
Mm.

419
24:51.870 --> 24:53.060
See you tomorrow.

420
24:53.720 --> 24:54.560
Sweet dreams.

421
24:55.770 --> 24:56.770
Good night.

422
25:13.200 --> 25:16.440
[The 66 Cottage]

423
25:27.120 --> 25:28.360
What would you like, Jane?

424
25:28.520 --> 25:31.000
Almond milk latte with no sugar? The usual?

425
25:31.630 --> 25:32.230
Right.

426
25:47.030 --> 25:49.750
Almond milk latte with no sugar?

427
25:50.730 --> 25:51.730
Oh...

428
25:52.040 --> 25:53.450
Oh, yes...

429
25:53.470 --> 25:56.630
And I'll have a cup of black coffee, please.

430
25:57.450 --> 25:58.920
Also no sugar.

431
25:59.280 --> 26:00.200
Alright.

432
26:02.570 --> 26:05.900
In case you're interested, we have a weekend promotion.

433
26:05.920 --> 26:09.740
You can write wishes and messages on postcards.

434
26:09.770 --> 26:13.140
They'll be displayed in the shop as a thank you to our first group of customers.

435
26:13.160 --> 26:14.610
Whoa...

436
26:14.630 --> 26:16.020
That's like...

437
26:16.130 --> 26:18.660
writing our names on temple roof tiles for merits.

438
26:18.680 --> 26:19.400
Yeah?

439
26:19.480 --> 26:20.010
Ow!

440
26:21.440 --> 26:22.340
Uh...

441
26:22.360 --> 26:23.790
That's such a lovely idea.

442
26:24.230 --> 26:25.730
I'll also have that one, please.

443
26:25.750 --> 26:26.750
Alright.

444
26:27.440 --> 26:29.030
We'll bring your order to your table.

445
26:29.050 --> 26:29.700
Thank you.

446
26:58.140 --> 26:59.140
Hey, Jane.

447
26:59.250 --> 27:01.310
It's a light activity for fun, not a final exam.

448
27:01.330 --> 27:02.770
Why are you taking it so seriously?

449
27:03.390 --> 27:05.010
I don't know what to write.

450
27:06.820 --> 27:08.230
So draw something instead.

451
27:11.730 --> 27:12.730
What should I draw?

452
27:14.540 --> 27:15.620
Ah.

453
27:15.850 --> 27:18.690
So you can draw anything, huh?

454
27:20.730 --> 27:22.130
Alright.

455
27:22.530 --> 27:23.930
You're asking for a challenge.

456
27:24.440 --> 27:25.440
I like that.

457
27:25.950 --> 27:27.490
Show me what you've got, then.

458
27:50.720 --> 27:51.720
Whoa!

459
27:51.940 --> 27:52.940
That's adorable.

460
27:53.370 --> 27:56.050
You're great at drawing, Jane.

461
27:56.740 --> 27:57.740
Of course.

462
27:57.840 --> 28:02.140
I was one of the top storyboard artists of my class.

463
28:02.650 --> 28:03.930
Whoa, Jane.

464
28:04.220 --> 28:06.080
Why haven't you told me about this before?

465
28:06.100 --> 28:07.160
Do you know how many times

466
28:07.180 --> 28:09.850
I've pitched my ideas to the team with simple stick figures?

467
28:10.040 --> 28:10.680
Gosh!

468
28:11.230 --> 28:13.510
It's embarrassing, you know?

469
28:13.530 --> 28:14.440
Ow.

470
28:15.060 --> 28:16.310
You've never asked me about it.

471
28:17.240 --> 28:20.110
I always ask you, "Is there anything I can help you with?"

472
28:20.130 --> 28:21.630
But every time you say, "No."

473
28:22.570 --> 28:24.120
And now you're complaining?

474
28:24.870 --> 28:26.130
You're right...

475
28:26.540 --> 28:27.540
Fine.

476
28:28.040 --> 28:29.040
It's my fault.

477
28:29.720 --> 28:30.930
I'm sorry!

478
28:31.340 --> 28:33.040
- Here. - Please forgive me.

479
28:33.450 --> 28:34.450
You wanna write anything?

480
28:35.760 --> 28:36.760
I don't think so.

481
28:37.330 --> 28:38.810
My handwriting is a mess.

482
28:38.930 --> 28:40.510
It'll ruin your drawing.

483
28:42.030 --> 28:43.440
I'll write it for you, then.

484
28:43.940 --> 28:45.330
What do you want your message to be?

485
28:49.430 --> 28:50.920
What should it be...?

486
28:54.140 --> 28:55.730
Oh...

487
28:58.930 --> 29:00.420
"JaabJane

488
29:00.830 --> 29:01.830
was here."

489
29:02.320 --> 29:03.120
How about that?

490
29:10.130 --> 29:11.540
How about...

491
29:11.640 --> 29:13.840
"Here, there was JaabJane."

492
29:14.730 --> 29:15.500
Sounds good?

493
30:00.740 --> 30:02.530
All done. Let's go.

494
30:03.640 --> 30:04.450
Huh?

495
30:05.430 --> 30:06.280
Oh.

496
30:06.300 --> 30:07.400
Yeah, let's go.

497
30:09.540 --> 30:10.540
Jane.

498
30:11.230 --> 30:12.940
Wait... Wait for me.

499
30:13.530 --> 30:14.530
Jane, Jane.

500
30:14.550 --> 30:16.740
[May what comes next be wonderful

501
30:16.760 --> 30:18.480
#JaabJaneWasHere]

502
30:19.650 --> 30:21.040
Oh. Come on, Sis.

503
30:21.060 --> 30:23.210
Why is our lead producer so headstrong?

504
30:23.230 --> 30:24.710
You said the meeting was postponed, no?

505
30:24.740 --> 30:26.730
Well, it was.

506
30:26.850 --> 30:28.850
From yesterday to today.

507
30:29.030 --> 30:31.480
Why didn't you tell me ahead of time?!

508
30:31.500 --> 30:32.380
I've got an appointment.

509
30:32.400 --> 30:34.940
I told you I'd have to leave the office early.

510
30:35.030 --> 30:36.340
Damn it...

511
30:37.630 --> 30:40.490
Aww. You may leave now, Khanoon.

512
30:40.520 --> 30:43.060
You can leave right away. Go ahead.

513
30:43.920 --> 30:45.530
- Can I? - Mm.

514
30:46.650 --> 30:49.390
You can leave, but don't come back again.

515
30:49.410 --> 30:51.540
Go ahead. Don't come here tomorrow either.

516
30:52.940 --> 30:55.090
- Ah! Ah! - Okay?

517
30:55.430 --> 30:56.940
Please, don't, Sis.

518
30:56.960 --> 30:58.080
I've learned my lesson, Sis.

519
30:58.100 --> 30:59.020
Don't say that, please.

520
30:59.040 --> 31:01.430
Don't hire a new DOP, please.

521
31:01.530 --> 31:02.430
Ugh!

522
31:03.140 --> 31:04.120
Jaab, how's it going?

523
31:04.140 --> 31:05.860
Have you come up with any ideas?

524
31:06.030 --> 31:08.410
I know that once the meeting was postponed,

525
31:08.430 --> 31:10.360
you wouldn't make any progress.

526
31:10.380 --> 31:11.620
That's what you do.

527
31:11.640 --> 31:14.320
No deadline, no progress.

528
31:14.830 --> 31:16.130
Come on, Sis.

529
31:16.150 --> 31:18.040
I just haven't put my ideas in the slides.

530
31:18.430 --> 31:19.730
But I can tell you all about it.

531
31:20.220 --> 31:21.630
Because I'm...

532
31:21.840 --> 31:24.160
not as irresponsible as you think.

533
31:25.390 --> 31:26.240
Mm.

534
31:26.340 --> 31:30.040
Good. It's great to see some progress.

535
31:30.060 --> 31:32.390
If changes were to be made,

536
31:32.410 --> 31:34.050
you could simply leave the slides untouched.

537
31:35.130 --> 31:36.150
What do you mean? Changes?

538
31:36.240 --> 31:38.200
I'll smack you in the mouth.

539
31:39.850 --> 31:41.440
What an inauspicious thing to say.

540
31:41.840 --> 31:43.150
I'm very confident

541
31:44.020 --> 31:45.730
with this draft.

542
31:45.940 --> 31:48.330
Huh. Are you sure?

543
31:48.360 --> 31:49.660
It's an MV for a sad song.

544
31:49.690 --> 31:52.090
I hope it doesn't turn into a wedding presentation like last time.

545
31:54.330 --> 31:55.840
Wedding, my ass!

546
31:58.930 --> 31:59.500
What?

547
31:59.580 --> 32:01.890
And when did you get that coffee? You didn't tell me to tag along.

548
32:02.710 --> 32:03.920
Jane also has one.

549
32:03.940 --> 32:05.800
You two didn't invite us to come along?

550
32:05.820 --> 32:07.060
Is there something going on between you?

551
32:12.240 --> 32:13.820
Uh...

552
32:14.670 --> 32:16.000
Pink Team!

553
32:16.020 --> 32:18.260
Let's... Let's start the meeting!

554
32:18.280 --> 32:18.710
Shall we?

555
32:18.730 --> 32:20.080
Come on, Jane.

556
32:20.930 --> 32:22.360
Come on. Let's move, Jane.

557
32:22.640 --> 32:24.140
- Hurry up, Jane. - Oh...

558
32:25.720 --> 32:27.020
Move, Jane.

559
32:27.680 --> 32:29.250
See? We work hard.

560
32:30.240 --> 32:30.890
Look at them...

561
32:30.910 --> 32:32.420
Hey. Move it, Jane.

562
32:39.250 --> 32:40.440
Really?

563
32:40.830 --> 32:41.900
Right?

564
32:42.550 --> 32:43.500
No wonder...

565
32:43.520 --> 32:44.520
I can sense it.

566
32:51.630 --> 32:52.630
Uh...

567
32:52.900 --> 32:53.900
Pun.

568
32:54.340 --> 32:54.710
Yes?

569
32:54.730 --> 32:57.290
Why "Pink Team"?

570
33:03.540 --> 33:05.520
It's a superstition.

571
33:05.830 --> 33:07.150
Like, spooky stuff.

572
33:07.340 --> 33:08.170
Huh?

573
33:08.950 --> 33:10.940
Well... Position-wise,

574
33:11.130 --> 33:13.080
Bew has the most power, right?

575
33:14.610 --> 33:17.520
But to get ideas approved easily and to diminish some of her authority,

576
33:17.930 --> 33:19.340
we agreed to name our group

577
33:19.640 --> 33:21.340
after the meaning of Chomphoo's name

578
33:21.620 --> 33:23.050
to undermine Bew's power.

579
33:23.450 --> 33:24.450
Is that true?

580
33:24.730 --> 33:25.690
Nope.

581
33:26.800 --> 33:28.020
Oh...

582
33:28.530 --> 33:30.320
I actually believed that.

583
33:30.730 --> 33:31.410
Well...

584
33:31.930 --> 33:33.320
During the New Year's party,

585
33:33.720 --> 33:36.220
we had to name our team for the lucky draw.

586
33:37.320 --> 33:39.450
We had to come up with a name when we were already drunk.

587
33:39.740 --> 33:41.120
So Jaab just blurted out a name.

588
33:42.340 --> 33:45.250
The color pink is pretty cutesy,

589
33:45.610 --> 33:47.430
and it suits our team.

590
33:51.420 --> 33:52.260
Oh...

591
33:53.530 --> 33:54.530
Not cutesy?

592
33:59.330 --> 34:00.730
Uh, Pun.

593
34:00.750 --> 34:01.420
Hm?

594
34:01.930 --> 34:03.740
About Jaab and Jane,

595
34:03.760 --> 34:04.240
I...

596
34:07.850 --> 34:09.350
Never speak about this.

597
34:10.040 --> 34:12.040
But Jane already...

598
34:12.240 --> 34:13.830
I told you. Don't bring it up.

599
34:14.850 --> 34:15.850
Let's get to the meeting.

600
34:17.930 --> 34:18.760
Come on.

601
34:32.230 --> 34:34.140
I think your ideas sound alright.

602
34:34.840 --> 34:36.070
I agree, Sis.

603
34:36.330 --> 34:37.670
Going through the past moments

604
34:37.690 --> 34:39.010
should devastate the viewers.

605
34:39.080 --> 34:40.370
Right?!

606
34:40.840 --> 34:42.410
That's what I'm aiming for.

607
34:43.430 --> 34:46.220
And when do you think it'll be ready, Jaab?

608
34:46.440 --> 34:48.380
I'll schedule the deadline with the client.

609
34:48.810 --> 34:49.810
Mm...

610
34:49.830 --> 34:50.930
I think...

611
34:50.950 --> 34:52.970
it should be ready in a few days.

612
34:52.990 --> 34:53.930
Mm.

613
34:54.100 --> 34:55.640
How about we schedule a date for scouting?

614
34:56.030 --> 34:57.400
We should include actual images, too.

615
34:57.420 --> 34:59.340
So the client will get a clearer picture. Okay?

616
34:59.440 --> 35:02.020
Also, I want you all to finalize all of the ideas.

617
35:02.040 --> 35:05.330
So I can request the first draw from the budget to keep our cash flow going.

618
35:06.340 --> 35:07.510
How about the day after tomorrow?

619
35:07.530 --> 35:08.770
Everyone's free, right?

620
35:09.660 --> 35:10.470
Mm, yeah.

621
35:10.840 --> 35:12.970
Do you want a van? I'll contact one.

622
35:13.240 --> 35:14.240
What do you think?

623
35:14.260 --> 35:16.700
Or do you want the gas money?

624
35:16.840 --> 35:18.220
Gas money sounds better.

625
35:18.240 --> 35:19.980
- So I can scoot when it's a wrap. - Mm.

626
35:20.040 --> 35:21.040
Agreed.

627
35:21.150 --> 35:24.130
I don't feel like driving back into the city, Sis.

628
35:25.140 --> 35:26.880
Okay, so that settles it.

629
35:26.900 --> 35:28.250
And... Ai,

630
35:28.270 --> 35:29.400
you're coming with the team.

631
35:29.420 --> 35:30.320
Go help Jane.

632
35:30.630 --> 35:31.890
Okay, sure.

633
35:32.440 --> 35:33.280
Anything else?

634
35:33.300 --> 35:34.050
I don't think so.

635
35:34.940 --> 35:36.060
- Nobody wants to bring up anything? - No.

636
35:36.080 --> 35:37.390
Right. We're all done here.

637
35:37.410 --> 35:39.090
- I'm fine with anything. - Okay.

638
35:39.110 --> 35:41.230
- Hey... - That's about it. Right, Sis?

639
35:54.710 --> 35:56.500
Are you two a couple?

640
35:57.340 --> 35:58.340
No.

641
35:58.630 --> 35:59.700
What makes you say that?

642
36:01.070 --> 36:02.410
I'm sorry.

643
36:02.430 --> 36:05.220
Uh... You two seem very close.

644
36:07.330 --> 36:08.950
Jaab and I are friends.

645
36:09.420 --> 36:11.570
He's my close friend.

646
36:16.050 --> 36:17.640
I'm actually

647
36:17.930 --> 36:20.040
interested in someone already.

648
36:29.780 --> 36:30.500
Jane!

649
36:30.650 --> 36:32.540
Look out! A shark!

650
36:34.640 --> 36:36.000
- Gosh, Jaab. Who's going to... - Nom, nom, nom.

651
36:36.020 --> 36:36.910
- Yeah. Take that, you shark. - Ow, Jane!

652
36:36.930 --> 36:37.640
Jane, Jane, Jane.

653
36:37.660 --> 36:38.550
Jane! Jane! Jane!

654
36:38.570 --> 36:39.910
Ow! I'm sorry!

655
36:43.240 --> 36:45.970
Ai, do you think Jaab can win Jane's heart?

656
36:48.230 --> 36:49.470
Win his heart?

657
36:49.860 --> 36:50.800
Mm.

658
36:51.280 --> 36:52.930
It looks possible, though.

659
36:52.950 --> 36:55.660
Jane is closer to Jaab than anyone else in the office.

660
36:56.440 --> 36:59.140
And they get along very well in so many aspects.

661
36:59.160 --> 37:00.230
Don't you think so?

662
37:00.920 --> 37:01.780
Pun.

663
37:02.420 --> 37:03.490
Mm.

664
37:03.650 --> 37:06.150
Uh... About Jaab and Jane,

665
37:06.690 --> 37:09.810
I don't think that's how it goes.

666
37:30.730 --> 37:31.620
Oh... Oh.

667
37:38.500 --> 37:40.600
Not only are you not helping,

668
37:40.810 --> 37:42.330
but you're also distracting me, Jaab.

669
37:42.800 --> 37:44.590
This is your own work, too.

670
37:45.200 --> 37:46.420
What?

671
37:46.600 --> 37:48.200
You said you wanted to help.

672
37:48.220 --> 37:49.820
Well, I'm letting you help me.

673
37:51.500 --> 37:53.460
This isn't "letting me help."

674
37:53.600 --> 37:55.520
This is "dumping your work on me."

675
38:02.190 --> 38:02.910
Well...

676
38:03.720 --> 38:05.660
I don't know how to help you.

677
38:05.910 --> 38:07.300
If I drew something,

678
38:07.320 --> 38:09.180
the work would end up like that one horse meme.

679
38:10.900 --> 38:11.810
What horse meme?

680
38:11.830 --> 38:12.610
Huh?

681
38:12.630 --> 38:14.420
You haven't seen it?

682
38:14.440 --> 38:15.500
The horse drawing meme.

683
38:15.520 --> 38:18.170
The body of the horse is beautifully sketched.

684
38:18.190 --> 38:19.690
But its head

685
38:19.710 --> 38:20.870
looks sloppy like...

686
38:20.890 --> 38:22.690
it was drawn by a kindergartener.

687
38:39.530 --> 38:40.110
How's that?

688
38:40.540 --> 38:41.330
Uh...

689
38:42.100 --> 38:43.100
Hold on, Jaab.

690
38:43.120 --> 38:44.750
What are you doing?

691
38:45.100 --> 38:47.190
Oh, I'm giving you a massage.

692
38:47.210 --> 38:48.250
In case your arm is tired.

693
38:48.710 --> 38:49.490
Okay?

694
38:50.320 --> 38:51.910
But you're moving my arm.

695
38:52.900 --> 38:54.490
The lines are all messy now.

696
38:55.200 --> 38:56.200
Oh...

697
39:02.370 --> 39:04.510
I can't do anything.

698
39:05.300 --> 39:06.300
Ugh...

699
39:06.900 --> 39:08.140
How the hell am I supposed to help?

700
39:21.830 --> 39:22.590
Jane!

701
39:23.200 --> 39:23.910
Hm?

702
39:24.920 --> 39:25.920
Jane!

703
39:27.990 --> 39:28.890
What is it, Jaab?

704
39:29.360 --> 39:30.920
Three... Four...

705
39:30.950 --> 39:33.310
♫Let's go, Jane, you've got this♫

706
39:33.330 --> 39:34.780
♫Let's go, Jane, you can do it♫

707
39:34.800 --> 39:36.760
- ♫Let's go♫ - Wait, wait, wait.

708
39:37.200 --> 39:38.200
What are you doing?

709
39:39.010 --> 39:40.090
I'm cheering you on, obviously.

710
39:40.110 --> 39:42.450
♫Let's go, Jane, you've got this♫

711
39:42.470 --> 39:44.500
♫Let's go, Jane, you can do it♫

712
39:44.650 --> 39:46.830
♫Let's go, Jane, you've got this♫

713
39:46.850 --> 39:48.990
♫Let's go, Jane, you can do it♫

714
39:49.010 --> 39:50.380
♫Let's go, Jane♫

715
40:57.900 --> 40:58.900
Jane...

716
41:01.200 --> 41:03.540
How about you continue the work tomorrow?

717
41:05.110 --> 41:06.620
I was about to wake you up.

718
41:06.920 --> 41:07.920
I wanted to tell you that...

719
41:08.430 --> 41:09.060
it's all done.

720
41:10.410 --> 41:11.410
Really?

721
41:19.510 --> 41:20.280
Here.

722
41:24.100 --> 41:25.360
I'm sorry, Jane.

723
41:26.490 --> 41:27.820
I feel really bad now.

724
41:28.000 --> 41:29.530
I didn't think that it would take this long.

725
41:29.720 --> 41:30.590
If I had known,

726
41:30.840 --> 41:33.100
I would've stuck to the stick figures.

727
41:35.300 --> 41:36.840
You're only starting to feel bad

728
41:36.860 --> 41:38.740
now that the work is done?

729
41:48.400 --> 41:49.150
And...

730
41:49.590 --> 41:50.800
what now, Jane?

731
41:51.010 --> 41:52.810
Are you heading home? Or...

732
41:52.910 --> 41:54.630
do you want to have a late dinner with me?

733
41:54.690 --> 41:56.420
It's my treat.

734
41:57.320 --> 41:58.900
Um...

735
41:58.920 --> 42:00.200
I'm heading home, probably.

736
42:00.890 --> 42:02.200
Oh, I see.

737
42:02.610 --> 42:03.610
Mm.

738
42:03.720 --> 42:04.510
Okay.

739
42:04.800 --> 42:05.560
Let's just say...

740
42:05.580 --> 42:07.580
I owe you a meal.

741
42:09.430 --> 42:10.620
- Okay? - Mm.

742
42:16.810 --> 42:17.810
What's so funny, Jane?

743
42:18.120 --> 42:18.990
Hm?

744
42:19.710 --> 42:21.440
I'm handsome, I know. But don't stare too often.

745
42:22.210 --> 42:23.490
Do you have a pet bird or what?

746
42:25.700 --> 42:26.700
I don't.

747
42:28.400 --> 42:29.290
See?

748
42:29.310 --> 42:31.110
Your hair looks like a bird's nest.

749
42:51.790 --> 42:52.790
Mm.

750
42:53.320 --> 42:55.790
Well, let me go grab my stuff.

751
42:57.420 --> 42:58.420
Right.

752
43:09.800 --> 43:10.800
Jane!

753
43:10.820 --> 43:12.920
My hair's messy again, Jane.

754
43:12.940 --> 43:15.190
Ow! There's a whole flock on my head, Jane!

755
43:15.220 --> 43:16.980
Help me fix it, please...

756
43:17.010 --> 43:17.740
Jane!

757
43:18.350 --> 43:19.600
Jane, wait up!

758
43:31.200 --> 43:32.020
What are you doing?

759
43:32.040 --> 43:32.990
Listening to some music?

760
43:33.320 --> 43:34.820
Oh, yeah.

761
43:34.840 --> 43:37.510
I want to recheck it quickly before sending the storyboard to the group chat.

762
43:40.000 --> 43:41.000
Do you want to...

763
43:41.310 --> 43:42.140
listen with me?

764
43:42.890 --> 43:43.550
Mm.

765
43:45.850 --> 43:47.150
Okay. Here.

766
44:04.660 --> 44:05.230
Uh... Jane.

767
44:05.900 --> 44:06.600
Hm?

768
44:08.620 --> 44:09.990
About our movie plan,

769
44:10.300 --> 44:12.700
there's a theater near Sukhumvit.

770
44:12.720 --> 44:14.260
- It's called... - Oh, is it "3sept"?

771
44:14.380 --> 44:15.100
What?!

772
44:15.300 --> 44:16.150
You know it?!

773
44:16.310 --> 44:17.060
Of course.

774
44:17.950 --> 44:19.500
I always went there back in my university days.

775
44:19.520 --> 44:22.940
It's peaceful there. So many good films, too.

776
44:23.020 --> 44:24.020
Whoa...

777
44:24.400 --> 44:25.240
You have great taste.

778
44:26.330 --> 44:28.340
So you like niche films, too?

779
44:28.700 --> 44:30.390
I used to go there with Min all the time.

780
44:31.240 --> 44:32.490
But after graduation,

781
44:32.510 --> 44:34.430
we parted ways for our jobs.

782
44:34.610 --> 44:35.780
So I completely forgot about it.

783
44:36.770 --> 44:37.740
- Right... - Oh.

784
44:38.310 --> 44:39.310
Now that I'm talking about it...

785
44:39.330 --> 44:41.110
I feel kinda nostalgic.

786
44:44.290 --> 44:45.290
How about...

787
44:46.420 --> 44:48.610
we go there sometime?

788
44:49.610 --> 44:50.380
Sure.

789
44:50.920 --> 44:51.820
Really?

790
45:01.100 --> 45:02.100
By the way,

791
45:02.120 --> 45:03.220
both of us...

792
45:03.490 --> 45:05.300
have so much in common, don't we?

793
45:07.020 --> 45:10.630
At a glance, it might seem like we wouldn't get along,

794
45:10.980 --> 45:11.980
but...

795
45:12.510 --> 45:14.510
we've got so much in common.

796
45:14.910 --> 45:15.910
Both of us.

797
45:18.110 --> 45:19.120
Agreed.

798
45:21.220 --> 45:22.220
And...

799
45:22.600 --> 45:25.110
do you believe in the chemistry between two people?

800
45:29.500 --> 45:30.950
Chemistry?

801
45:31.190 --> 45:32.270
Mm.

802
45:32.900 --> 45:34.400
Like the chemistry...

803
45:34.710 --> 45:37.110
between two characters?

804
45:39.320 --> 45:40.320
Exactly.

805
45:44.060 --> 45:45.010
Right...

806
46:07.700 --> 46:08.700
- Jane. - Hm?

807
46:08.910 --> 46:10.970
Whose phone should we use to call for a ride?

808
46:11.910 --> 46:12.800
It's fine.

809
46:12.820 --> 46:14.190
Someone's picking me up.

810
46:14.510 --> 46:15.590
You wanna tag along?

811
46:16.100 --> 46:18.500
I might bring a friend with me, I mentioned that.

812
46:19.220 --> 46:20.220
Whoa...

813
46:20.680 --> 46:22.020
Who is it?

814
46:22.040 --> 46:23.300
Is it your family?

815
46:23.590 --> 46:24.340
Or is it Min?

816
46:26.410 --> 46:27.410
His name is Mon.

817
46:32.600 --> 46:33.550
Mon?

818
46:35.420 --> 46:36.600
I've been talking to him.

819
46:45.510 --> 46:46.680
You've been talking?

820
46:47.390 --> 46:48.380
Mm.

821
46:54.280 --> 46:55.900
There he is. Perfect timing.

822
47:20.600 --> 47:21.780
Did I keep you waiting?

823
47:22.010 --> 47:23.380
I came as quickly as I could.

824
47:23.900 --> 47:26.030
Not at all. We're just here, too.

825
47:28.520 --> 47:29.520
Jaab, right?

826
47:30.600 --> 47:32.000
You're tagging along with us, yeah?

827
47:32.290 --> 47:33.600
Jane told me about you.

828
47:42.410 --> 47:43.410
Oh...

829
47:44.600 --> 47:46.250
I don't want to be trouble.

830
47:46.800 --> 47:48.120
What? Why?

831
47:50.090 --> 47:51.680
Uh... Well,

832
47:51.700 --> 47:53.510
my mom just texted me

833
47:53.720 --> 47:54.900
to come home right away.

834
47:55.900 --> 47:56.900
Oh, really?

835
47:58.200 --> 47:59.200
I guess...

836
48:00.220 --> 48:01.220
this is where we call it, then?

837
48:01.800 --> 48:02.800
Mm.

838
48:04.220 --> 48:05.220
Mon,

839
48:06.730 --> 48:07.340
have a good one.

840
48:07.360 --> 48:08.410
You, too.

841
48:24.710 --> 48:25.710
Wait, Jaab.

842
48:43.400 --> 48:44.800
You forgot to give this back to your friend?

843
48:45.900 --> 48:47.450
Oh, right.

844
49:14.210 --> 49:15.900
Jane told me so much about you.

845
49:17.010 --> 49:18.010
Thank you

846
49:18.900 --> 49:20.100
for being his close friend.

847
49:23.710 --> 49:24.710
It's my pleasure.

848
49:26.910 --> 49:27.910
Should we get going?

849
49:29.220 --> 49:30.220
Bye-bye, Jaab.

850
49:30.620 --> 49:31.810
See you, Jane.

851
50:20.410 --> 50:21.410
Hello, Mek.

852
50:27.900 --> 50:28.900
Damn it...

853
50:29.810 --> 50:31.490
I'm not the one...

854
50:32.870 --> 50:34.640
Mek, I'm not the one.

855
50:34.940 --> 50:36.310
I've been imagining it on my own.

856
50:37.000 --> 50:38.590
I've been imagining it from the start!

857
50:42.890 --> 50:45.390
Chemistry is the connection between characters.

858
50:45.410 --> 50:47.690
It's a feeling that lights up

859
50:47.910 --> 50:49.900
when two people are together.

860
50:50.100 --> 50:53.000
Chemistry turns ordinary scenes into special ones.

861
50:54.510 --> 50:57.200
It happens on its own

862
50:57.410 --> 50:58.800
without an explanation.

863
50:59.110 --> 51:00.190
It's not an exact science.

864
51:00.500 --> 51:01.900
No rules set in stone.

865
51:02.520 --> 51:04.080
It's like an eruption in my heart

866
51:05.300 --> 51:07.220
that I've been imagining...

867
51:07.700 --> 51:08.920
all on my own.

868
51:31.010 --> 51:33.200
Shit... My heart is broken.

869
51:33.300 --> 51:34.460
Broken, my ass.

870
51:34.480 --> 51:35.480
You two were never even a thing.

871
51:35.890 --> 51:36.920
That guy is just someone Jane's talking to.

872
51:37.010 --> 51:38.550
They're not official yet. You have a chance, no?

873
51:38.570 --> 51:39.920
I'll lose either way.

874
51:40.050 --> 51:41.210
Wouldn't it be better...

875
51:41.240 --> 51:43.400
if I stayed like this so that Jane would still be around?

876
51:43.720 --> 51:45.080
What should I do, Jane?

877
51:45.280 --> 51:46.440
I'm...

878
51:46.490 --> 51:47.870
so fucking in love with you.

879
51:48.920 --> 51:49.900
Before I can... [I'm sorry]

880
51:49.920 --> 51:51.560
call somebody "a friend,"

881
51:51.710 --> 51:53.400
it's really hard for me, Jaab.
